      "writtenOn": "2014-07-02T16:45:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The order does matter. \nat least when SPI is \"idle\", are we sure that the DATA pin is never high ? *(that\u0027s unclear to me, I had issue in the past but also bits were remaining in the FIFO)\nWe really don\u0027t want to have TX_DATA high and TX_EN still Hi-Z.\n\nif gpio_set_alternate is too slow, maybe we need an open coded version here, that\u0027s just one register to set here.",
      "parentUuid": "84d6ed80_be7ad1fc",
      "revId": "1aa67779f0de76eff3cd4ea718b46d134c7509ed",
